From 4868e6ee6a1b11e26aa68b4c993b396d8189b711 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: A2Tools-patch <patch@localhost>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 03:14:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Plugins: the player row on its own header button; video
 opacity that works on KDE

- The video's opacity is drawn into the picture (a GL pass after mpv), so it
  works where the window manager ignores a widget's own opacity (KDE).
- A widget playing a video stays shown when the plugins button or the plugin
  window hides the plugin's other widgets.
- The header's TV button shows or hides the player row ("Player row"); the
  row opens by itself when something starts to play, and lists players that
  are idle (dimmed). A manifest's ui.overlay can leave out its own header
  button ("button": false).
---
